{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/derio-net/super-fr/pulls/527","id":4591837296,"node_id":"PR_kwDOR-_5V88AAAABEbHgcA","html_url":"https://github.com/derio-net/super-fr/pull/527","diff_url":"https://github.com/derio-net/super-fr/pull/527.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/derio-net/super-fr/pull/527.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/derio-net/super-fr/issues/527","number":527,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Five defects found driving #508's Test Plan live: unbriefed resolve, a false model, a guard that blocked fr-goal's first action, venv thrash, and an unobserved parity claim","user":{"login":"YiannisDermitzakis","id":10046982,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDQ2OTgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10046982?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YiannisDermitzakis","html_url":"https://github.com/YiannisDermitzakis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YiannisDermitzakis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YiannisDermitzakis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YiannisDermitzakis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YiannisDermitzakis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YiannisDermitzakis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YiannisDermitzakis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YiannisDermitzakis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YiannisDermitzakis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YiannisDermitzakis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Five defects found while driving #508's post-merge Test Plan live (evidence: #521). One fix per commit, each with a reproduced failure and a single confirmed root cause **before** any code — the trail, including rejected ideas and one correction of my own false statement, is in `docs/superpowers/journals/debug/2026-09-21-508-live-test-plan-defects.md`.\n\n| | root cause | fix | proof |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **C3** | `_resolve_member` guarded the group and the *other* units, never the unit itself — so a never-briefed unit went absent → `done` with **no attempt** (no holder, no cost). The flat path always had the rule. | refuse a unit `advance` never briefed, *after* the one-writer refusal | 2 red → green. One existing test had **encoded** the defect; the 2026-09-09 spec's write-claim passage is why changing it is a correction, not a weakening |\n| **C2** | `_open_dispatch` derived the tier's `model` for **every** attempt, including ones with no `agent_type` (\"the orchestrator\") — work no tier ever touched | derive only for dispatched work; a *reported* `--model` is kept | red on `'claude-opus-5' is None`. **Not a labelling quibble:** `implemented/runs/…unit-record-unification-r2.yaml` on `main` credits 7 inline reviews to a model that did not perform them |\n| **C4** | the bash guard's allowlist predates `fr run start` entering isolation itself — so fr-goal's \"first action\" was denied from the base clone | allow `start` **only**; it does not retire the sentinel | hid because it only bites when the repo already has *someone's* worktree (else the #341 self-heal deletes the sentinel first) — now pinned by a test that fails when the allowance is removed |\n| **C5** | bind-mounted worktree + uv defaulting to `<project>/.venv` on both sides: one path, two operating systems, each side deleting the other's venv on every alternation (~26 MB re-download in the container) | scaffold emits `containerEnv.UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT=.venv-container` for uv profiles; this repo's two profiles carry it | **live, twice**: container rebuilt from the committed profile, 3 host/container alternations, **0 deletions**, host venv untouched, git never sees the dir |\n| **C1** | the claim protocol was live-verified on Claude Code (dispatch returns an id at once), then *declared* for OpenCode, whose task tool **blocks** and returns the id with the result | fr's behaviour was not wrong — what it **said** was. New parity row `dispatch-holder-identity`; skill + explainer corrected | 7 red → green; explainer baseline re-render byte-identical, page diff = the new paragraphs only |\n\n## Independent review\n\nDispatched through `superpowers:requesting-code-review` with no session history; findings handled through `receiving-code-review` (each verified in code or by experiment first). **No Critical, no legitimate flow broken. 11 findings: 10 fixed, 1 left as by-design.** The ones worth your attention:\n\n- **fr-goal never said to `advance` before `review-phase`** — the prose that *produced* C3, and which would have tripped the new refusal once per phase. Fixed in the skill and both mirrors, token-tested.\n- **I stated a false mechanism**: that `fr isolation exec` is a plain `docker exec`. It is `devcontainer exec`. `containerEnv` is still right, for a reason I had not checked. An earlier commit message on this branch still carries the wrong sentence; the journal has a correction record below it.\n- **Absolute → relative env path.** The reviewer said a shared absolute path destroys packages across projects. **That did not reproduce** (0 uninstalls, probed in the container). What the same probe *did* show: project `a` importing a package only `b` declared. Relative paths are resolved per project by uv.\n- **My new parity row repeated the defect it corrects** — `claude-code: enforced` for something that is nameable, not enforced. Now `advisory`.\n\n## Deliberately not fixed (recorded, not dropped)\n\n- **The #341 self-heal retires a *fresh* pipeline's sentinel** in a repo with no linked worktree — the first base-clone command of a new pipeline makes the guard inert for that session. Needs a way to tell \"new\" from \"orphaned\": a design decision.\n- **The real closing of C1**: `fr-opencode-plugin` already tells child sessions from top-level ones, so it could claim on the child's first tool call. New CLI affordance + plugin behaviour, and not live-verifiable from Claude Code. Noted in the parity cell itself.\n- **Cursors already carrying C2's false model** are not repaired — a repair would be guessing; archives are frozen by rule.\n\n## Operator notes\n\n- **Existing containers must be recreated** to pick up C5 (a container's env is fixed at creation). Profiles already scaffolded in consumer repos are not rewritten.\n- **`main` moved twice under this PR** (#513, then #524). Every conflict was in a generated or lockstepped file and **none was text-merged**: `main`'s side taken, mine re-applied through the real tools (bump-version, rows re-appended by block, reports regenerated). When `matrix.yaml` *did* text-merge cleanly it was verified, not trusted — the result is exactly the union of both parents, all 60 rows `main` changed carried. The same will be needed against #521, whichever lands second; I'll do it on request.\n- **Three of this PR's own matrix line anchors had rotted** — my review fixes added lines above them after I recorded them, and nothing reports a stale anchor. Repaired; all eight land on their `def`. The general gap is not closed here.\n- Version **4.13.1** (patch, on top of #513's 4.13.0). 4 acceptance rows added, all `ci`; two were narrowed in review to what is actually true and actually CI-verified.\n\n## Verification\n\nFull suite as CI sees it (`CLAUDE*` unset): **4044 passed, 80 skipped, 0 failed**, coverage **92.32%** (over the tree merged with #513; #524 is docs-only and was covered by the 830 artifact/acceptance/tripwire tests). `ruff format --check`, `ruff check`, `mypy` (146 files), `bump-version --check`, both mirror generators, `fr harness parity --check`, `fr validate artifacts` (34), `fr acceptance check` + `report --check` (178 rows), `fr workflow check fr-goal`, `fr journal check --scope debug` — all clean.\n\n- [x] CI green on this branch\n- [x] Explicit review approval\n- [x] No commits pushed since that approval\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","created_at":"2026-09-21T13:09:02Z","updated_at":"2026-09-21T13:42:10Z","closed_at":"2026-09-21T13:42:08Z","merged_at":"2026-09-21T13:42:08Z","merge_commit_sha":"537d8b8e897a8c7d7516d4f576d00600d1b71111","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/derio-net/super-fr/pulls/527/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/derio-net/super-fr/pulls/527/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/derio-net/super-fr/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/derio-net/super-fr/issues/527/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/derio-net/super-fr/statuses/ccc79c61efe7d65d27e4a19e927009b8e4d761ab","head":{"label":"derio-net:fix/508-live-test-plan-defects","ref":"fix/508-live-test-plan-defects","sha":"ccc79c61efe7d65d27e4a19e927009b8e4d761ab","user":{"login":"derio-net","id":252884407,"node_id":"O_kgDODxK1tw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/252884407?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/derio-net","html_url":"https://github.com/derio-net","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derio-net/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derio-net/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derio-net/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derio-net/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derio-net/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derio-net/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derio-net/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derio-net/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/derio-net/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"repo":{"id":1206909271,"node_id":"R_kgDO